{"resource":{"id":"ka-hffZzLjCSwU","title":"Préparation des Alcynes","s":"chemistry","t":"","p":"khan","f":"video","c":"Chimie organique","u":"Alcènes et Alcynes","d":445,"l":"progressive","v":"hffZzLjCSwU","url":"https://fr.khanacademy.org/science/organic-chemistry/alkenes-alkynes/naming-preparation-alkynes/v/preparation-of-alkynes","b":0},"descriptionHtml":"Lorsqu'un alcyne vrai (ou terminal) est produit, une base forte peut capter le proton et il y a formation d'un ion alcynure. Il faut alors ajouter une source de proton (comme H2O) pour régénérer l'alcyne vrai.","related":[{"id":"ka-jsdoubba_cM","title":"Alcynes : Acidité et Alkylation","f":"video"},{"id":"ka-6KDn1rpaWOs","title":"Réduction des Alcynes","f":"video"},{"id":"ka-Qe4TIWrW2D4","title":"Hydrohalogénation des Alcynes","f":"video"}],"attribution":"Khan Academy et ses contributeurs","license":"CC BY-NC-SA","sourceUrl":"https://fr.khanacademy.org/science/organic-chemistry/alkenes-alkynes/naming-preparation-alkynes/v/preparation-of-alkynes"}